# Add patterns of files dvc should ignore, which could improve
# the performance. Learn more at
# https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/dvcignore

# NOTE: `**/cropped/` used to be ignored here, on the reasoning that the crops
# are regenerable from the raw photos + code. True in principle, but nothing
# automated it -- crop_tray.py was not a pipeline stage -- while training reads
# *only* the crops. The result was a pipeline that could not run anywhere the
# crops did not already sit in the working tree (see Phase 9 in
# EXPERIMENTS_LOG.md). Crops are now a `crop` stage output under data/cropped/,
# so DVC tracks them properly and the ignore is gone.

# Python bytecode. `coffeecv` is a dep of the train stage, so without this every
# run rewrites .pyc files, changes the directory hash, and makes DVC report the
# stage as changed when no source file changed.
__pycache__/
